 to be active in acrosomal vesicle and motile cilium. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8NA54","text":"Adapter protein that anchors the radial spoke 1 (RS1) complex to the A microtubule of outer doublet microtubules in axonemes (PubMed:36355624). The triple radial spokes (RS1, RS2 and RS3) are required to modulate beating of the sperm flagellum (PubMed:36355624). May play a role in inhibiting signaling via MAPK1/ERK2 and MAPK3/ERK1 (PubMed:36355624). Additionally, may play a role in the functioning of cilia (By similarity). Not required for the functioning of tracheal or ependymal cilia (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}